d *proposed* in the report.   A new heuristic strategy may be registered in `satisfiability/heuristics.py`   as a named option; it may not become the default of anything. - **Every split groups by file ∪ MOSP-graph isomorphism class**   (`learning.fingerprint.union_groups`). - **Nodes, not seconds**; seconds beside them; a censored call is a lower   bound, never a missing value; SAT cost is counted in conflicts. - **State the size range every conclusion covers.** Corpus 6,376 at 9–134;   campaign 37,800 at 10–40, 6,747 at 50–75, a 5-per-cell sample at 100; item   07 adds one certified cell at 100. Nothing below 100 is evidence about   125 × 125 except through a stated extrapolation. - Every number in a report is regenerated by a command named in that report. - Findings that rest on a handful of instances are re-certified for those   instances (`solve_mosp_exact`, never `solutions_dir=None`) before being written.  - **Compute**: check `pgrep -f benchmarks.recertify`; if it is running, its   cores are not yours. 32 cores total; use up to 16 here. Each iteration has   a hard 3-hour wall-clock cap enforced by the driver; items 06 and 07 price   their runs before starting (`learning.cost_model` for 07) and sample if the   full run will not fit, saying so.  ## Current Focus `reports/ml_nature_plan_3.md` §1: thirteen items in the order written. Items 01–03 are cheap closures; 04–06 narrow soundness above 40 customers; 07–08 extend the ridge to 100; 09–10 explain the ridge; 11 and 12 equip the two proof problems; 13 is the reserve.  ## Target Problems (in order) See `iterations.md`. Work on exactly ONE unchecked item per iteration.  ## Acceptance Criteria (per item) - [ ] Code lives under `learning/` (or `lean/` for item 12, `satisfiability/`       for a registered heuristic or a flag) with a module docstring saying what       question it answers and how to run it; runnable as `python -m learning.<name>`. - [ ] A section appended to `reports/ml_nature.md` (continuing the numbering,       §28 onwards) with: the question, the method, the baseline, the table(s),       the finding in one paragraph, the size range covered, the kill       criterion's verdict where the plan states one, and the regenerate command. - [ ] `python -m pytest tests/ -q -x` passes (~85 s). New code that computes a       quantity gets at least one test on a tiny hand-checkable instance; a new       flag on the search gets a test that the default path is byte-for-byte       unchanged and a test that the flag never changes a `decide` status. - [ ] The item is marked `- [x]` (done) or `- [!]` (blocked, with a reason in       PROGRESS.md) in `iterations.md`. - [ ] No regressions, no changes to solver defaults, nothing written to       `solutions/`. Generated instances and witnesses go under       `learning/data/ensemble/` (committed; total under ~150 MB apparent).  ## Completion Conditions An item is DONE when either: 1. **Solved**: meets all criteria and the report section is written, OR 2. **Blocked**: documented in PROGRESS.md with the specific blocker. Items 05,    11 and 12 may end with a precise statement of what cannot be done and why;    that is a deliverable, not a failure.  ## Context - **Key files**: `learning/differential.py` (the harness; `--stage drawn`),   `learning/graph_story.py` (relabel, recover), `learning/relabel_portfolio.py`,   `learning/cost_model.py` (pricing for item 07), `learning/ensemble.py` and   `learning/upward.py` (the campaign; resumable), `learning/scale_test.py`   (`fit_scaling`, `scale_nodes.csv`), `learning/hardness_map.py`,   `learning/ridge_theory.py` (§25's candidates and peaks), `learning/extremal.py`   and `learning/treewidth.py` (the adversary and exact treewidth),   `learning/conjecture.py` (the validity oracle over 50,949 instances),   `learning/distil.py` (the two-key rule, `HYPOTHESES`), `learning/corpus_sweep.py`,   `satisfiability/customer_search.py` and `.c` (the search; `dominance_filter`   in the C is where the fix lives; `reports/better_move_bug.md` §7),   `satisfiability/heuristics.py` (`STRATEGIES`, `least_cost_node`, `restricted_dfs`),   `satisfiability/mosp_solver.py` (`decide_mosp`, the SAT path; `SAT_BACKEND`),   `satisfiability/mosp_encoding.py`, `learning/proofs.py` (DRAT),   `learning/degeneracy.py` (the lattice oracle), `lean/MOSPFormalization/Reduction.lean`   and `Sandwich.lean`, `literature/becceneri_yanasse_soma_2004_method_mosp_cutting.pdf`   (MCNh pseudocode §4, worked example Table 1 and Fig. 2),   `literature/plosone_2018_pagerank_mosp.pdf` (Frinhani's MCNh column),   `recertify/results.json` (the 125 × 125 counts; all pre-fix). - **Data**: `solutions/*.json` (read-only here); `learning/data/ensemble/`   (`results.csv`, `results_upward.csv`, `scale_nodes.csv`, `differential*.csv*`,   `portfolio*.csv*`, `theorem2.csv.gz`, `recover*.csv*`, `relabel.csv.gz`);   `learning/data/canonical.csv`, `instances.csv`. - **Testing**: `python -m pytest tests/ -q -x`. - **Dependencies**: `learning/requirements.txt`; new packages only behind soft imports.  ## Important Notes - Do NOT run `benchmarks.csearch`, `benchmarks.recertify`, `benchmarks.overnight`   or any sweep that writes to `solutions/`. - Do NOT edit `CLAUDE.md`; the loop's owner folds findings in afterwards. - Do NOT rewrite existing report sections; append. If a finding contradicts an   earlier one, say so in the new section and leave the old one in place. - Commit nothing yourself; the driver commits after tests pass. - You are running in print mode: **ending your turn ends the session.** Two   loop0003 sessions ended their turn waiting on a background run and had to   be redone. Run studies in the foreground or poll them in a bounded loop, and   do not stop until the report section, PROGRESS.md and iterations.md are   written. If a run will outlast the session, write the section from what has   settled, mark the rest censored, and say so. - When stopping a background process, match its PID or an anchored patter