{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfUDmKxrxmwuMdxvE62eM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 01 is done. Everything the driver needs is written; nothing was committed and nothing touched `solutions/`.\n\n**Result.** Over all 6,376 certified instances, the two-key rule seeds Chu & Stuckey's restricted DFS better than the LightGBM policy on every statistic, and faster.\n\n| strategy | exact | mean overshoot | worst | better / worse vs `cs-dfs` | ms mean |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `cs-dfs` | 84.5% | 0.241 | +10 | — | 29.5 |\n| `rule+cs-dfs` | 94.2% | 0.092 | +8 | 780 / 12 | 16.7 |\n| `learned+cs-dfs`, file ∪ class folds | 92.1% | 0.128 | +8 | 602 / 19 | 20.6 |\n\nHead to head the rule seed beats the learned seed on 263 instances and loses on 80, and leads in every size band and every collection. The LightGBM dependency question no longer exists: the learned seed is dominated by a model-free strategy of the same cost class. Making `rule+cs-dfs` the upper bound where `cs-dfs` is used today is proposed in the report and not applied.\n\n**Side finding.** The 2026-09-22 file-grouped split leaked. Grouping by file ∪ isomorphism class puts every Chu & Stuckey, Faggioli–Bentivoglio, SCOOP, Challenge, Wilson and Shaw file into one fold trained on Harvey and Simonis only, and the learned seed's lead over `cs-dfs` drops from 709 / 13 to 602 / 19 under it.\n\n**What was written.**\n- `satisfiability/heuristics.py`: `two_key_closing_order`, strategies `rule` and `rule+cs-dfs`, registered and the default of nothing.\n- `learning/rule_seed.py`: trains the union-fold models, runs five sweeps through `learning.corpus_sweep` (new `--model-dir`), times in-process, writes `reports/rule_seed_tables.md`.\n- `tests/test_rule_seed.py`: 11 tests, including the chain, a 4-cycle that pins the tie-break direction, the Becceneri–Yanasse–Soma 2004 Table 1 example (printed sequence simulates to 4, the optimum), and the sweep's ledger row into a temporary ledger.\n- `reports/ml_nature.md` §28, `PROGRESS.md` iteration 1, item 01 marked done in `iterations.md`.\n\nFull suite: 1,083 passed, 2 skipped, 1 xfailed in 83 s. One caveat in the report: milliseconds were measured beside 9 recertify workers, so absolute values are about 1.5× those in `reports/learning.md` and only the ratios are the claim. Twelve items remain, so no `LOOP_COMPLETE`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":738,"cache_read_input_tokens":175651,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":738,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e888114f-204a-4797-a011-93927a3593bf","uuid":"f1657d5d-aee0-4a5d-bfe9-f2d61d2f66b0","timestamp":"2026-09-27T15:59:07.250Z","request_id":"req_011CfUDmGehCw34UqqZ47rSy"}
